# Line endings.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, so a plain `git clone` there
# rewrites every text file to CRLF. That is fine for prose and fatal for the
# rest of this repo:
#
#   * `vdm` and the hooks are bash scripts. A shebang line ending in CR makes
#     the kernel look for an interpreter literally named "bash\r", and the
#     error ("bad interpreter: no such file or directory") names a file that
#     plainly exists — hours of confusion for one invisible byte.
#   * The tests lift functions out of dashboard.mjs by slicing on "\n}\n".
#     With CRLF that needle never matches, and five tests fail with
#     "updateAccountState is not defined" while the code is perfectly fine.
#
# So: LF for everything the machine reads, regardless of platform. install.ps1
# is the exception — PowerShell is happy either way, but a Windows user opening
# it in Notepad should not see one long line.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.ps1 text eol=crlf

*.png binary
